CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ empty pack: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ first: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ second value-initialized: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
A trailing non-type template parameter pack that occurs only in the type
of a parameter whose argument is a braced-init-list was left as its
unassigned placeholder instead of being deduced empty, so the substituted
parameter type could not be formed and the candidate was dropped ("found
no match").
